          "Record the opening count by owner and channel, because a single total can hide a queue concentrated in one person. Report the number of cases that could not be classified and the reason, rather than forcing them into a category. If the definition of client report timeliness changes, keep the old and new values side by side for the transition period. Record the extraction date and the queue filter so another reviewer can reproduce the population count. Keep the measurement note short enough to read with the case and specific enough to support the reported client report timeliness. The October 28 team roster note should distinguish a missing timekeeping exception from a confirmed negative."
