          "Each case needs the source, the observation time, the field supported, the owner, and the reviewer. If a field is derived, record the formula and the source fields used to calculate it. Use one row per case and one column per required field; do not bury evidence in a long free-text note. Pilot the dictionary with two reviewers and compare their classifications before the main sample. If the evidence is sensitive, record the approved reference and access path rather than copying the content. The October 28 team roster recovery test should record the restore point and the timekeeping exception rate result.",
